<title>USA: Navistar approves funding for Mexican plant.</title>
<headline>Navistar approves funding for Mexican plant.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Navistar International Corp said Wednesday its directors authorized a $167 million capital expenditure for construction of a truck assembly plant in Mexico.</p>
<p>Several sites are under evaluation.  </p>
<p>The new facility will be designed to meet projected demand for trucks in Mexico and Latin America.</p>
<p>Navistar said it currently serves Mexico through a 23-location dealer network, a parts distribution center and a contract manufacturing arrangement.</p>
<p>It also has a technology and licensing relationship with Mexican truck maker Dina Camiones that will expire in March 1998.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
